  <title>7.10.1: Graphs of Linear Equations</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01903</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.10.1: Graphs of Linear Equations</md:title>
    <md:uuid>1de22a5d-1c08-4a1a-8252-6402dba1cc63</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Warm Up Activity</title>
<para>Here is a graph of the equation \(y=8-2x\).</para>
<para><figure><media alt="Insert Alt Text"><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/5343dd297c92f5f2465ea997ddc0588e0870d044"/></media></figure></para>

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Where do you see the 8 from the equation in the graph?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>The 8 in \(y=8-2x\) means the graph intersects the \(y\)-axis at 8. The \(y\)-intercept is (0,8).</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Where do you see the –2 from the equation in the graph?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>The –2 is the slope of the line. You can see it, for example, by looking at \((0,8)\) and \((1,6)\). When \(x\) increases by 1, \(y\) decreases by 2.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->

<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="a68ddf4b-ca4f-408c-94b0-a432193eb080" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="0" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--Q3-->
  <exercise data-content-id="2ce36a44-7afd-4ec4-b992-74d1eaaf0c8c" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="4">
    <problem>
      <para>What is the value of \(x\) for the \(x\)-intercept of the graph? How does this relate to the equation?</para>
      <para>Enter your answer here.</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The \(x\)-intercept is \((4,0)\). The 4 is the solution of \(8-2x=0\).</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
